Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:32:56 +0300
Subject: Compress textures at upload on Mesa too (texcompress)

With GL_EXT_texture_compression_s3tc the engine compresses textures from texcompress pixels up (default 1024) at upload, but not on Mesa: usetexcompress stayed 0 there, from the days Mesa had no S3TC encoder. Ours has one (nv30 exposes S3TC; DXT1 is encoded on the SPUs by libspeq), and VRAM is scarce on the PS3, so the texcompress cvar now decides on Mesa as elsewhere. RGBA textures become DXT5, which Mesa encodes on the PPE.

diff --git a/engine/rendergl.cpp b/engine/rendergl.cpp
--- a/engine/rendergl.cpp
+++ b/engine/rendergl.cpp
@@ -533,7 +533,7 @@ void gl_checkextensions()
 #ifdef __APPLE__
         usetexcompress = 1;
 #else
-        if(!mesa) usetexcompress = 2;
+        usetexcompress = 2;
 #endif
         if(dbgexts) conoutf(CON_INIT, "Using GL_EXT_texture_compression_s3tc extension.");
     }
